id: pm-ckb8w5
title: Schedule corpus and policy fixture keepers after parallel contract workers
description: "Two full-source coverage runs at unchanged assertion deadlines expose worker-contention failures in the surface replication fixture checks; the runs also expose the ten-thousand-item aggregate and cold governance-read keepers. All seven targeted recovery files pass together (155 tests) with four workers. Reuse the established serial lifecycle-performance cohort for these three expensive files, preserving their original source/input populations and budgets."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: quality-gate,runner-allocation,test-reliability
created_at: "2026-10-20T12:27:13.226Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T13:19:40.805Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T13:19:39.861Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T13:19:39.861Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "All three files are excluded from parallel contracts and included exactly once after that project with one worker. Existing 10-second governance, 30-second aggregate and 120-second policy test limits, retry policy, fixture cardinality and canonical full-source 100 percent coverage remain unchanged. A real config negative control fails before allocation is changed; focused, full coverage and CI evidence are retained."
goal: Make quality verdicts measure the intended SDK and policy behavior under qualified execution.
objective: Allocate expensive corpus and policy keepers consistently with the existing sequential project.
value: Preserve strict gate signal without rewarding timeout inflation or nondeterministic retries.
why_now: Both canonical coverage runs during the current admission-safety delivery hit unchanged contention-sensitive fixture deadlines.
parent: pm-bj7rq0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Move the existing surface replication, aggregate membership and governance read files into the single-worker lifecycle-performance cohort after contracts. Add a failing-before membership keeper and recurrence policy without changing assertions, inputs, timeouts, retries or coverage denominator."
expected_result: Each expensive keeper runs exactly once after parallel contracts and still detects real behavior regressions at its original limits.
actual_result: Allocation negative control fails before config change. Revised six-file suite passes80 tests; linked four-file suite passes23 tests within original deadlines. Hosted head211b1c8 passes complete coverage with100% statements/branches/functions/lines and no fixture timeout. Earlier failed full local receipts and the separate qualified startup-budget issue remain documented. Graph/integrity and docstring checks pass after typed relationship corrections; final combined-head CI is required before merge.
